# 🇨🇦 Nunavut — The Ultimate Travel Guide

## Welcome to Nunavut

Nunavut is Canada's newest and largest territory — a vast Arctic land of frozen oceans, towering mountains, ancient landscapes, and living Indigenous traditions.

Created in 1999 through the Nunavut Land Claims Agreement, Nunavut is a place where Inuit culture, Arctic wildlife, and one of the most dramatic environments on Earth come together.

With no roads connecting most communities, Nunavut offers a rare kind of travel: remote, authentic, and deeply connected to the land.

Here, travelers can experience the Arctic Ocean, see polar bears and narwhals, explore ancient archaeological sites, witness the northern lights, and learn from Inuit communities whose relationship with the Arctic stretches back thousands of years.

Nunavut is the ultimate destination for explorers seeking the extraordinary.

